        "original_id": "b0c519e4-eafb-55e6-9313-5f1f3da86f2d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Shep Meyers, Coleman Hawkins, Lenny Bruce, Steve Allen, Redd Foxx, Henny Youngman, Johnny Carson, Woody Herman, Art Pepper, Conte Candoli, Don Joham\n- Places: Sahara Hotel, Las Vegas\n- Roles: pianist, composer, arranger, conductor, jazz tenor saxophonist\n\nFacts:\n- Coleman Hawkins was born on November 21, 1904, and he died on May 19, 1969.\n- Coleman Hawkins was an American jazz tenor saxophonist nicknamed Hawk and sometimes Bean.\n- Shep Meyers was born on October 5, 1936, and he died on July 18, 2009.\n- Shep Meyers was an American pianist, composer, arranger, and conductor.\n- Shep Meyers served as conductor for the bands of Lenny Bruce, Steve Allen, Redd Foxx, Henny Youngman, and Johnny Carson during his residency at the Sahara Hotel in Las Vegas.\n- Shep Meyers played with Woody Herman, Coleman Hawkins, Art Pepper, Conte Candoli, and Don Joham.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
